# One line ending in the repository, whatever the contributor's OS.
#
# Without this, files committed from Windows arrive with CRLF and files
# committed from macOS or Linux arrive with LF, so the first clone on the other
# platform shows a whole-file diff on every one of them and `git blame` stops
# being useful. Normalising in the repository and checking out natively is
# git's documented answer.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
